{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363569-when-do-you-use-extended-actions","id":1363569,"title":"When do you use extended actions ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-27T00:49:56-08:00","id":1363569,"title":"When do you use extended actions ?","content":"Suppose your solar wants to climb one of Nexus' towers, 50 meters tall.<br /> <br /> Do you use an extended action ? Do you ask for multiple rolls intertwined with twists while climbing the tower (You happen to pose your feet on a trapped block ! You start losing balance while this part of the wall crumbles, what do you do ?) ? Is it just a simple roll ? I guess most of the time it will depend on the context, say if I have absolutely no follow up for this climbing and there is no real narrative interest besides &quot;I climb this tower because it's cool&quot;, I won't make it a 30 successes extended roll taking place over 30 mns, but how you approach this ? I got the feeling I'm not using extended rolls often enough, sometimes resorting to simple rolls, but then it makes the awkward situation where one roll is a bit of all-or-nothing, while I think a more &quot;step by step&quot; approach would allow for more drama and engagement from the players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T01:03:07-08:00","id":1363571,"title":"","content":"An extended roll is just a normal roll with a tighter bell curve, a cost multiplier on charms, and that (quite damningly) takes a lot longer for what <i>still</i> boils down to an all-or-nothing weighted coin toss. Why <i>would</i> you use one? <br /> If you want &quot;more drama and engagement&quot;, have a series of distinct rolls each with a different success/failure result. Strength+Athletics to get past the start of the climb where years of would-be climbers have worn the stone smooth. Perception+Stealth to not be attacked by the predatory birds roosting in a crevice (and Stamina+Resistance to see how much it hurts if you fail). Stamina+Athletics to not have to turn back. Charisma+Presence to tell the paranoid elemental that you <i>really</i> aren't there for anything involving it and just want to go up past it. Strength+Brawl when you realize the elemental wasn't convinced and that handhold starts holding back. Stamina+Athletics to have enough left in you to finish the climb.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T01:30:34-08:00","id":1363579,"title":"","content":"I was basically thinking of what you just wrote except these are the steps inside the extended roll of Athletics + Stamina or Dexterity to climb the tower, but I guess this might not be necessary. I was just trying to think of some applications of extended rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T02:00:01-08:00","id":1363584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363569-when-do-you-use-extended-actions?p=1363579#post1363579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was just trying to think of some applications of extended rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't really see the point of them, to be blunt. They just mean more dice against a larger Difficulty, which doesn't add anything interesting. <br /> What benefit does an extended roll have over just omitting all but the last roll, or rolling once at the start and using margin of success to determine how long it takes? <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25764-vwllss-trnt-prncss","name":"vwllss trnt prncss","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"244"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T02:25:22-08:00","id":1363586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363569-when-do-you-use-extended-actions?p=1363584#post1363584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see the point of them, to be blunt. They just mean more dice against a larger Difficulty, which doesn't add anything interesting.<br /> What benefit does an extended roll have over just omitting all but the last roll, or rolling once at the start and using margin of success to determine how long it takes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, but the system present them, so I'm trying to figure out their different applications. There are some subsystems that use extended rolls, and I think in some places they could be useful as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T07:08:16-08:00","id":1363615,"title":"","content":"I think extended rolls are useful <i>if</i> there's some drama in the question of &quot;how long does it take to accomplish this task?&quot;. For example, if there's a sorcerer on top of the tower casting a big spell like Rain of Doom, it becomes relevant to determine exactly how quickly the Athletics-specialist in the party can scale it and try to interrupt. Or the party is sailing across the Neck, trying to reach Skullstone before the Silver Prince can execute their friend. Basically, there needs to be some kind of narrative consequence for failure.<br /> <br /> The craft system's extended rolls are okay, in my opinion, because they do have built-in consequences for failure: each roll costs craft XP, and, of course, if you reach the terminus before you succeed, you can't build that artifact at all. Other extended rolls, I'd generally be more cautious about using. If there's no major consequences for failure, either of a single roll or the whole thing, there's little point to using them, in my opinion. If you're just checking how long it takes someone to do something for timekeeping purposes, it's simpler and less boring if you just call for one roll, and use margin of success/failure to estimate how long it takes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T07:09:07-08:00","id":1363616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vwllss trnt prncss</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363569-when-do-you-use-extended-actions?p=1363584#post1363584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't really see the point of them, to be blunt. They just mean more dice against a larger Difficulty, which doesn't add anything interesting. <br /> What benefit does an extended roll have over just omitting all but the last roll, or rolling once at the start and using margin of success to determine how long it takes? </div> </div> </div> </div>One thing it does is let you modify your strategy and more spending as you go. So if you\u2019re climbing a tower and you totally flub the first roll you can turn up the heat and full excellency it with 3 supplemental charms on the next two rolls to catch up. <br /> <br /> It also has the effect of just extending a scene and affecting the pacing of the session. Instead of just one roll and then you\u2019re at the top and we move on the multiple rolls would be played out and individually stunted as dancing along a crumbling parapet and leaping up to the next tier, and then tossing your grappling line up into a window and flinging yourself up after it, getting to the point where the tower splits in two at the top and wall jumping between the spires.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T07:18:55-08:00","id":1363619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363569-when-do-you-use-extended-actions?p=1363616#post1363616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing it does is let you modify your strategy and more spending as you go. So if you\u2019re climbing a tower and you totally flub the first roll you can turn up the heat and full excellency it with 3 supplemental charms on the next two rolls to catch up.<br /> <br /> It also has the effect of just extending a scene and affecting the pacing of the session. Instead of just one roll and then you\u2019re at the top and we move on the multiple rolls would be played out and individually stunted as dancing along a crumbling parapet and leaping up to the next tier, and then tossing your grappling line up into a window and flinging yourself up after it, getting to the point where the tower splits in two at the top and wall jumping between the spires.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I agree with you, I think villas trnt prncss solution is basically the same as you propose, except it's closer to a sort of skill challenge where the player has to use different skills along the way to succeed. <br /> <br /> I agree with Kelly Pedersen that one should use extended rolls if there is a meaningful consequence for failing the roll, not just time. <br /> <br /> Right now, I'm thinking like this : Start the extended roll, put a challenge at each interval that can complexity the extended roll (arrived at the middle of the climbing, if you fail the roll to notice the unstable wall, you might have a malus for the next extended Athletics roll) and keep going until the climbing is full. <br /> <br /> The only &quot;downside&quot; I see about this is it's quite usual for Solars to totally destroy extended rolls with 15+ successes. Which means the quite good description and stunt could be done in a single roll from the player, directly succeeding at the task. I know solars are so good and stuff so it's acceptable, but if at some point I'd like to stay a bit longer on the awesome stunt of the solar climbing the tower, I could not make it an extended roll, and let him go through few challenges requiring different skills. <br /> <br /> Does anyone have sole kind of Chart for what difficulty extended rolls should be ? I usually consider 5-10 to be rather easy rolls (always with Terminus 5), and then medium is 10 - 20 and then difficult is all the way up to 30. Any comments ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T07:47:49-08:00","id":1363625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363569-when-do-you-use-extended-actions?p=1363619#post1363619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I agree with you, I think villas trnt prncss solution is basically the same as you propose, except it's closer to a sort of skill challenge where the player has to use different skills along the way to succeed.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could always have an extended roll that takes multiple different kinds of pools, although that might not make a ton of sense. If you\u2019re scaling a mountain and absolutely kill the athletics roll that maybe shouldn\u2019t let you skip the social roll.<br /> <br /> Then again if you\u2019re interacting with a mountain god or something maybe you should be using the social system for it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363569-when-do-you-use-extended-actions?p=1363619#post1363619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have sole kind of Chart for what difficulty extended rolls should be ? I usually consider 5-10 to be rather easy rolls (always with Terminus 5), and then medium is 10 - 20 and then difficult is all the way up to 30. Any comments ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well the difficulty on the roll should be from 1-5 depending on how heroically difficult the task is. Other than that I think you\u2019re fairly right to go 10-30 range. The goal number shouldn\u2019t really be a measure of difficulty though, more just how much stuff there is to do. I think you\u2019re about right in the 10-30 range though. 15-20 is about where I\u2019d go most of the time for extended tasks, it\u2019s almost impossible to do them in one roll but also not so hard that they\u2019d take more than 2-3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T07:49:14-08:00","id":1363627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363569-when-do-you-use-extended-actions?p=1363619#post1363619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right now, I'm thinking like this : Start the extended roll, put a challenge at each interval that can complexity the extended roll (arrived at the middle of the climbing, if you fail the roll to notice the unstable wall, you might have a malus for the next extended Athletics roll) and keep going until the climbing is full.<br /> <br /> The only &quot;downside&quot; I see about this is it's quite usual for Solars to totally destroy extended rolls with 15+ successes. Which means the quite good description and stunt could be done in a single roll from the player, directly succeeding at the task. I know solars are so good and stuff so it's acceptable, but if at some point I'd like to stay a bit longer on the awesome stunt of the solar climbing the tower, I could not make it an extended roll, and let him go through few challenges requiring different skills.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you definitely have to calibrate the difficulty of the challenge to the abilities of the characters. Note, I'm <i>not</i> advocating changing the difficulty of tasks based on which character is attempting them - climbing a 30-foot stone tower with lots of missing bricks to provide hand- and foot-holds is equally easy for a mortal child and a thousand-year-old Dawn with Supernal Athletics. What I <i>am</i> suggesting is that the ST needs to make sure to establish scenery that will be adequately challenging. If the tower to be climbed is one of the glass spires of Chiaroscuro, two thousand yards tall, with razor-sharp edges that will count as environmental hazards on every roll, that's something that's likely to actually call for that Dawn's incredible skill. <br /> <br /> The idea of calling for other types of rolls is not a bad one either. I see there as being two ways to implement that kind of thing. First, incidental hazards or or challenges, things that might impede completing the task but not stop it entirely, will generally call for a secondary roll. In your example of the unstable wall, I'd call for a (Perception + [Awareness or Craft]) roll to spot it and, if failed, apply the penalty to subsequent rolls to climb. The other sort of different roll is where the interruption is basically impassable with the &quot;standard&quot; Ability. In that case, it's appropriate to call for the different pool to be used for the extended roll itself. For example, when climbing that 2000-yard glass tower, at the midpoint there's a magical field of glass blades swirling around the tower's circumference, barring passage. The climber's (Strength + Athletics) pool can't help them now, getting through is a question of (Perception + Dodge), to spot the gap and move through it fast enough. The climber has to roll that until they get enough threshold successes added to the pool to be considered past it, at which point they can go back to rolling (Strength + Athletics).<br /> <br /> In most cases of these kind of secondary/alternate rolls, I'd use total successes accrued to measure placement of things. Let's say climbing the tower will require 50 total successes. The unstable wall becomes visible at 10 successes, and if you fail to spot it, the difficulty increase applies until you reach 15 successes, meaning a couple of poor rolls could mean you're stuck with it longer. The spinning blade point, on the other hand, is reached once you achieve 25 successes, and from that point on, until you achieve 30 successes, you're rolling (Perception + Dodge) instead.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone have sole kind of Chart for what difficulty extended rolls should be ? I usually consider 5-10 to be rather easy rolls (always with Terminus 5), and then medium is 10 - 20 and then difficult is all the way up to 30. Any comments ?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think &quot;difficulty&quot; is harder to pin down with extended rolls. A challenge that needs 10 successes total, but has a terminus of 2 and a base difficulty of 5, is going to be a <i>lot</i> harder than one that requires accumulating 50 successes, but has a base difficulty of only 1 and no terminus at all. You've got to tweak all three variables to get an accurate guess of the difficulty.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T08:44:34-08:00","id":1363629,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363569-when-do-you-use-extended-actions?p=1363625#post1363625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You could always have an extended roll that takes multiple different kinds of pools, although that might not make a ton of sense. If you\u2019re scaling a mountain and absolutely kill the athletics roll that maybe shouldn\u2019t let you skip the social roll.<br /> <br /> Well the difficulty on the roll should be from 1-5 depending on how heroically difficult the task is. Other than that I think you\u2019re fairly right to go 10-30 range. The goal number shouldn\u2019t really be a measure of difficulty though, more just how much stuff there is to do. I think you\u2019re about right in the 10-30 range though. 15-20 is about where I\u2019d go most of the time for extended tasks, it\u2019s almost impossible to do them in one roll but also not so hard that they\u2019d take more than 2-3.</div> </div> </div> </div>1) Yeah I didn't think of that, but that's plain simple. for some unknown reasons I was thinking about another WoD system where I believe that your terminus is influenced by your skill in the ability used.<br /> <br /> 2) Thanks for the clarification I misused difficulty instead of goal number, but you got my back. I think 15-20 is usually hard enough for a little challenge for the stronger exalts, what I'm wondering is how to adjust the difficulty. I find it to be the hardest point, it's not like Sorcerous workings where every parameter offer a very clear signification in gameplay and choose for the players.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1533_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1533\" data-vbnamecard=\"1533\">Kelly Pedersen</a> I'm with you on your first part.<br /> <br /> I really do not like your second part, because despite you being right from the point of view of the system, I think it could really help to consider only one parameter, because else it makes everything very complicated. For example, I would only rarely play with Terminus because I think it has effects on the difficulty that are a bit harder to calculate and think of in play. I think putting Terminus almost always at 5 is a good solution (even if there will be corner cases where it doesn't make sense). Difficulty and goal number are a bit easier to tackle down I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T09:00:59-08:00","id":1363632,"title":"","content":"I once called for a one round interval extended action to determine how fast the Dawn could burn down a gate with rapid Fiery Arrow Attacks while under retaliatory fire, with an ammo check or two along the way under the assumption that the more successes he rolled each round the more arrows he\u2019d just fired (though I only charged him one FAA use per roll).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-27T09:21:15-08:00","id":1363642,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chausse</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1363569-when-do-you-use-extended-actions?p=1363629#post1363629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really do not like your second part, because despite you being right from the point of view of the system, I think it could really help to consider only one parameter, because else it makes everything very complicated.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's true that playing with the terminus probably complicates things more than adjusting difficulty or required successes. As a rule of thumb, I'd definitely say that sticking with a terminus of 5 is best whenever the timeframe of the challenge isn't set by other factors. If the Circle is racing across the sea in time to stop the execution of their friend, for example, you know that the deadline is 5 days from now, and it's fine to say that each interval is 1 day, while if the deadline was 10 days away, the interval would be 2 days instead. But there are a number of circumstances where I think you've got to mess with the terminus. To return to the &quot;climbing a tower while the sorcerer at the top casts a spell&quot; example, I wouldn't set a fixed terminus in that case at all. Instead, I'd have the sorcerer roll Shape Sorcery actions for each interval, while the climber rolled their skill, and the &quot;terminus&quot; would be determined by whether or not the sorcerer had accumulated enough successes to cast the spell.<br /> <br /> Or consider a challenge that happens in combat time - there's a big barrel of firedust placed at the base of a fortification wall, and somebody's got to rush over there before the trail of firedust that's being used as a fuse burns up to the barrel and sets it off. Using an interval other than a combat round is awkward, since it would mean that the people racing the fuse would be either rolling multiple times per round, or less than once a round, depending on the length of the fuse, and saying &quot;it will take 5 combat rounds for the fuse to run&quot; is implausibly long, and would virtually guarantee that the characters could make it anyway, eliminating the drama. So I'd set a terminus of, say, 3 combat rounds in that case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Interested in chatting with other Exalted fans online? Join us on the <a href=\"https://discord.gg/kGsyF5jhdy\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted Discord server</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1533-kelly-pedersen","name":"Kelly Pedersen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"929"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}